  "live_records": {
    "q-974": {
      "dom_id": "step-q974",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Given that $\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot {3}^{x}=5,$ find the value of $x$ rounded to $3$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot {3}^{x} & =5 \\\\ {3}^{x} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take ${log}_{3}$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{x} & =2 \\\\ {log}_{3}⁡({3}^{x}) & ={log}_{3}⁡(2) \\\\ x & ={log}_{3}⁡(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(2)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(3)}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx≈0.631\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
